namespace StockFeed.Landing;

/// <summary>
/// THE SEAM EVERY LANDING MECHANISM ENDS UP SENDING — the exact counterpart of <c>RunSendEmail</c> in the
/// automation folder, and it exists for the same reason. A webhook, a table the warehouse writes, and a poll of
/// their API are three different pieces of infrastructure that must produce one identical effect; without a
/// named seam each grows its own copy of the translation and only one copy gets tested.
///
/// Its field names are THE WAREHOUSE'S, deliberately. This record and
/// <see cref="StockFeed.Contracts.StockNoticed"/> are the only two places their vocabulary is allowed to exist,
/// and the second only exists because the model declares the foreign event's shape. Naming these members after
/// our domain would put the rename in the transport, where nothing on the model claims it.
///
/// WHAT IT IS NOT: an event of ours. It is never appended to our store. <see cref="StockFeed.Slices.StockFeed.StockTranslator"/>
/// handles it, translates it, and issues a command; the only thing that gets persisted is what we decided.
///
/// **The first version of this folder had an IngestStockNoticeHandler here that appended the foreign event to
/// our Stock stream, folded a Received[] array to dedupe it, and then woke a trigger off it with a Marten
/// subscription.** All of that is gone, and the reasoning is in the README under "what persisting the foreign
/// event cost". The short version: our event store is append-only, so a foreign schema written into it is in
/// our history for ever — which is the coupling a translation exists to prevent, installed by the thing meant
/// to prevent it.
///
/// TWO THINGS THAT DESIGN PROVIDED STILL HAVE TO COME FROM SOMEWHERE, and both do:
///
///   the durable record of what they said   the transport's inbox already holds it, with dead-lettering. It is
///                                          pruned, which is the right lifetime for a message and the wrong one
///                                          for history — so nothing that must be permanent depends on it
///   dedupe across redeliveries             the noticeId carried on our OWN event, folded by the decider. One
///                                          correlation value, not their schema
/// </summary>
public sealed record IngestStockNotice(
    Guid ProductId,
    Guid NoticeId,
    int Quantity,
    long Sequence,
    DateTimeOffset NoticedAt);
